window.BO_I18N.en = {"meta.title":"BIMopen — Free BIM modelling","ui.skip":"Skip to content","nav.viste":"Views","nav.funzioni":"Features","nav.formati":"Formats","nav.agenti":"Automation","nav.roadmap":"Roadmap","nav.scarica":"Download","nav.manuale":"Manual","nav.faq":"FAQ","cta.prova":"Try it in your browser","hero.ai":"AI-generated image","hero.four":"Design. Coordinate. Check. Document.","hero.lead":"BIMopen is free BIM software that will be released as open source (MIT/Apache). Model walls, doors, windows and floors once: plans, 3D view, schedules and IFC files all come from the same model and always stay in sync.","hero.gh":"GitHub · not public yet","fact.1":"No account, no subscription","fact.2":"IFC4 export","fact.3":"Experimental .rvt import","fact.4":"Browser, Windows and Linux · macOS coming","hero.kicker":"Free · multilingual · open source soon","hero.h1":"You draw the building,<br><em>the project writes itself.</em>","ui.p":"A side rail, command search with Ctrl+K, tool cards, the element panel and view thumbnails, light and dark. If you prefer a ribbon, choose the Classic style in Options: the commands are the same. The pictures show the interface in the language you chose.","car.1.t":"BIMopen dark","car.2.t":"BIMopen light","car.3.t":"Classic","car.4.t":"Touch PC","car.5.t":"Tablet landscape","car.6.t":"Tablet portrait","car.7.t":"Phone","car.8.t":"Browser","car.1.c":"The default style: rail, tool panel, command search and strip of views. Pick the theme in <b>Options › User Interface › Theme</b> or with the moon in the top bar.","car.2.c":"The same style in the light theme: switch between the two with the sun or the moon in the top bar. Commands and shortcuts stay the same.","car.3.c":"Tabbed ribbon, options bar, Properties palette and Project Index, for those used to working this way. <b>Options › User Interface › Interface › Classic</b>.","car.4.c":"For touch monitors and pens: palettes by category and controls big enough for a finger. <b>Options › User Interface › Touch mode › Always</b>.","car.5.c":"Touch mode on a tablet in landscape. It turns on by itself on Android and in browsers used with a finger: <b>Touch mode › Automatic</b>.","car.6.c":"On a tablet in portrait the properties step aside to leave room for the drawing; <b>Properties</b> in the top bar brings them back.","car.7.c":"On a phone the drawing takes the full width and five buttons at the bottom open views, families, tools, properties and commands. Automatic on Android and in narrow browsers.","car.8.c":"The same application in the browser, nothing to install (WebGPU or WebGL2): <b>Try it in your browser</b>. Your files stay on your computer.","viste.kicker":"One model, every view","viste.h2":"Change a wall: the plan, 3D and takeoff change too.","viste.p":"In BIMopen you don't draw lines but building elements with their own properties. Views are different readings of the same model, so they never need to be realigned by hand.","viste.h3a":"Plans, sections and elevations","viste.pa":"Cut walls with poché, door and window symbols, levels and grids with bubbles. For every level and every section, exportable as SVG and PNG.","viste.h3b":"3D view","viste.pb":"GPU-accelerated real-time navigation: orbit around the selection and zoom towards the cursor, transparent glazing, one-click element selection.","tab.mat":"Material","tab.m1":"Porous clay block","tab.m2":"Reinforced concrete","tab.m4":"EPS (external insulation)","tab.m3":"Hollow-block slab","tab.m5":"Wood fibre (roof)","tab.tot":"Total (16 materials)","viste.h3c":"Schedules and takeoff","viste.pc":"Configurable schedules for thirteen categories and a layer-by-layer material takeoff. They open as views beside plans and 3D, edit the model and follow it, go on sheets and export as CSV.","fun.kicker":"Features","fun.h2":"The tools you need every day","fun.p":"The BIM design workflow: levels and grids, then envelope, partitions, openings and floors.","f1.h3":"Layered walls","f1.p":"Wall types with finish, insulation and structure layers. L corners, T junctions and crossings resolve themselves.","f2.h3":"Hosted doors and windows","f2.p":"They sit in the wall, cut it and follow it when it moves. Width, height, sill, leaves and swing direction are parameters.","f3.h3":"Floors from walls","f3.p":"One click creates a floor on the outer perimeter of the level's walls, or you sketch it point by point.","f4.h3":"Instance and type properties","f4.p":"Constraints, dimensions and identity data for every element. Editing a type updates all its instances.","f5.h3":"Snaps and temporary dimensions","f5.p":"Snapping to endpoints, midpoints and intersections, ortho mode and lengths shown while you draw.","f6.h3":"Command line","f6.p":"Every action is also a command you can type, for example <code>WA</code> for a wall and <code>DR</code> for a door. Undo is unlimited.","fmt.kicker":"Open formats","fmt.h2":"Your projects stay yours","fmt.p":"BIMopen speaks the open BIM standard and is understood by other software, without locking you into a vendor.","fmt1.h3":"IFC4 export","fmt1.p":"Walls with their material layers, openings cut into the walls, doors and windows filling them, floors, roofs, stairs, railings, curtain walls, rooms and furniture, with types, properties and quantities. The file opens in any BIM software that reads IFC.","fmt2.h3":"Import of .rvt files: experimental","fmt2.p":"Today it reads only the project name and the level names. To exchange models, use IFC4. The reader is the open-source rvt library (Apache 2.0 licence).","fmt2.nota":"Walls, doors, windows and floors of .rvt files are not read yet.","fmt3.h3":"Database native format","fmt3.p":"A single database file: saving writes only the new and changed elements, with backup copies and save reminders. If the computer stops, the unsaved work comes back when the project is opened again. It exports to and imports from readable JSON, to compare and keep under version control.","fmt4.h3":"Drawings and tables","fmt4.p":"Plans as vector SVG at the chosen scale, images of plans and 3D, sheets printed to vector PDF, schedules and takeoffs as CSV.","ag.kicker":"Automation and artificial intelligence","ag.h2":"You can drive it by typing, too","ag.p":"Every button is a command, so BIMopen can be driven by repeatable scripts or by an AI assistant.","ag.l1":"A command line at the bottom of the window: type from anywhere.","ag.l2":"<code>bimopen-cli</code> for conversions, scripts and exports without a user interface.","ag.l3":"An <abbr title=\"Model Context Protocol\">MCP</abbr> server for AI agents, which can also render views to check their own work.","rm.kicker":"Project status","rm.h2":"In development, in the open","rm.p":"BIMopen is young. It already works for modelling simple buildings; the road to full professional use is public.","rm.full":"Full roadmap","dl.kicker":"Try it","dl.h2":"Get started now","dl1.h3":"In the browser","dl1.p":"Nothing to install: you need a recent browser (Chrome, Edge, Firefox or Safari) with WebGPU or WebGL2. BIMopen opens in the language chosen on this site, and your files stay on your computer.","dl1.btn":"Open BIMopen","dl2.h3":"For your computer","dl2.p":"Test builds for Windows 10/11 and Linux, to download: partial and not final, only for trying the program. The macOS version is coming.","dl3.h3":"Source code","dl3.p":"The code will be published under the MIT or Apache 2.0 licence, your choice: you will be able to use, study, modify and redistribute it, including for professional work. We are working on it.","faq.kicker":"Frequently asked questions","faq.h2":"Frequently asked questions","faq1.q":"How much does it cost?","faq1.a":"Nothing. BIMopen is free of charge and will be released as open source (MIT/Apache): no paid licences, no subscriptions and no accounts, even for professional use.","faq2.q":"Does it open .rvt files?","faq2.a":"Not usefully yet: the .rvt import is experimental and today reads only the project name and the level names. To exchange models with other BIM software, use IFC4, the open standard. BIMopen does not save in the .rvt format, which is closed.","faq3.q":"Where do my projects go?","faq3.a":"To your computer. Even in the browser version the model stays in the page, and saving downloads it as a file. This website uses no cookies and no tracking.","faq4.q":"Can I use it for a real project?","faq4.a":"For studies and simple models, yes: you model walls, floors, roofs, stairs and curtain walls, lay views out on sheets with a title block and print them to PDF, and the project file recovers your work after a crash. Ceilings, phases, loadable families and DWG export are still missing: you can follow their progress on the roadmap.","faq5.q":"What language is the program in?","faq5.a":"In Italian, English, German, French, Spanish and Arabic, right to left. On first start it uses the system or browser language; you can change it from the 🌐 menu at the top. This website is available in the same six languages.","faq6.q":"How can I contribute?","faq6.a":"By trying it and reporting problems and requests, or by contributing Rust code. Translations of terms and test models are also welcome.","fin.h2":"Your next project, in open BIM.","fin.p":"Open the sample house, move a wall and watch the plan, 3D and takeoff update together.","fin.altre":"More options","foot.lic":"To be released as open source (MIT/Apache)","foot.claude":"Built with","foot.codice":"Source code coming soon","foot.marchi":"Autodesk® and Revit® are trademarks or registered trademarks of Autodesk, Inc. BIMopen is an independent project, not affiliated with, sponsored or endorsed by Autodesk®; the names are used only to indicate the formats and workflows BIMopen is compatible with. IFC is a standard of buildingSMART International.","meta.desc":"BIMopen is free BIM software that will be released as open source (MIT/Apache): walls, doors, windows, floors, roofs and stairs in a single model, with plans, sections, 3D, schedules, PDF sheets and IFC4 export. In the browser and on your computer.","ui.sezioni":"Sections","ui.tema":"Change theme","car.label":"The BIMopen interfaces","car.prev":"Previous interface","car.next":"Next interface","viste.alt1":"Ground floor plan with hatched cut walls, doors with their swing, windows, grids, and rooms coloured by use with their legend","viste.alt2":"3D view of the sample house with its gable roof","viste.tab":"Material takeoff of the sample house, the five largest materials by volume","ag.code":"Example of BIMopen commands","ui.top":"Back to top","lb.label":"Enlarged picture","lb.close":"Close","lb.prev":"Previous picture","lb.next":"Next picture","rp.meta.title":"BIMopen roadmap — Status and next steps","rp.kicker":"Roadmap","rp.h1":"Where we are, <em>where we are going</em>","rp.lead":"BIMopen covers, command by command, the features of professional BIM software for architecture. Every feature was compared option by option with the expected behaviour: the steps, in order of priority, and the coverage percentages come from there. A step counts as done only when its commands have been tried in the interface, on the desktop and in the browser, the way a designer uses them, and are covered by automated interface tests.","rp.stat.avail":"features available","rp.stat.steps":"planned steps","rp.stat.cmds":"commands already working","rp.stat.lang":"languages, Arabic included","rp.toc.next":"Next version","rp.toc.avail":"Available","rp.toc.steps":"Steps","rp.toc.cov":"Coverage","rp.toc.out":"Out of scope","rp.next.kicker":"Next test version","rp.next.h2":"0.1.0-alpha.6","rp.next.p":"These are the features planned for the next test version.","nx.imperial":"Imperial units: feet and inches with fractions, decimal feet and inches, square and cubic feet, values typed as 5'-6 1/2\", an imperial project template","st.todo":"To do","nx.identity":"New identity: the cube and the program's colours on the site, in the manual and in every icon","st.done":"Done","nx.rvt":"The .rvt import described as what it is, with a note in the program when only the name and the levels are read","nx.stair_sketch":"Stair by sketch: risers and treads in the right order where the boundaries join, checked on screen from several viewpoints","nx.realistic":"Realistic visual style: physical sky, the sun's disc, dawn, sunset, night, the moon and the stars","rp.av.kicker":"Available today","rp.av.h2":"What already works","rp.av.p":"All of this can be tried right away in the browser, with a sample house.","rm1.ul":"<li>Levels, grids, walls, doors, windows, floors</li><li>Rooms, dimensions, text and tags</li><li>Plans, sections, elevations, 3D, schedules, takeoff</li><li>IFC4, SVG, PNG, CSV; experimental .rvt import (project name and level names)</li><li>Desktop, browser, command line, MCP</li><li>Interface in six languages, Arabic included</li><li>Several view windows: tile, cascade, replicate</li><li>View scale, cut heights, detail, 3D graphic styles</li><li>Sheets with title block, vector PDF printing</li><li>Hip, gable and flat roofs; walls attached to roofs</li><li>Crop region, hide and isolate elements</li><li>Selection with TAB and chains of walls, filter, Select All Instances; dragging in every view with joined walls stretching; move, copy, rotate, align with padlock, offset, mirror, linear and radial repeat in series, trim/extend, split, scale, fix</li><li>Components: furniture and plumbing fixtures, in schedules and IFC</li><li>Visibility and Graphics and styles by category</li><li>Detail lines, filled regions and masking regions</li><li>Type management: edit assembly of layers, purge unused</li><li>Project units</li><li>View filters</li><li>View templates</li><li>Segmented sections with adjustable far clip; detail views</li><li>Linear and angular dimensions, temporary dimensions, EQ and lock constraints</li><li>Stairs by run with landings, and railings, in plan, 3D, schedules and IFC</li><li>Area plans and color schemes with a legend</li><li>Detail components, repeating details, insulation and free 2D views</li><li>Curtain walls with grids, mullions and panels, in plan, 3D, schedules and IFC</li><li>Several plans per level, views duplicated (with detailing too) and renamed, saved 3D views</li><li>Walls with alignment, height or depth, continue, offset and flip</li><li>Project materials and fill patterns: shaded colour, surface and cut patterns, per layer and per category</li><li>Configurable schedules as views: fields, filters, sorting and grouping, totals, formulas, key schedules and material takeoffs, project and shared parameters; tiled with the other views, they edit the model and follow it; on sheets, in view templates and between projects</li><li>Project file as a database: saves only what changed, recovers work after a crash, backup copies, JSON export</li><li>Line weights by view scale, editable line patterns, subcategories of the styles by category and thin lines</li><li>Navigation: zoom towards the cursor, orbit around the selection, windows tiled by order of use, context menus in every view, views dragged onto sheets</li><li>User manual in six languages, on the web and in PDF, also opened from the program with F1</li><li>Orientation cube with compass, menu and home view, key tips with Alt, a quick access toolbar and keyboard shortcuts you set, exported and imported as XML</li><li>No tool changes the view by itself: where it cannot work, «Go to View» asks which view to open</li><li>Previews in 3D too: walls as solids with their temporary dimension, floors sketched on their level, doors, windows and components following the cursor</li><li>Opening IFC2x3 and IFC4 files: walls, floors, doors, windows and rooms become native elements, the rest generic models</li><li>Framing elevations on grids and note blocks</li><li>Every tool tried in plan, elevation, section and 3D: mirror and repeat in series in sections and elevations too, curtain wall tools and Pick Lines in 3D too</li><li>Two-letter shortcuts typed in the view, in both styles; snap overrides for the next point, typed or from the right button, with a message where they do not work; a «Snaps…» window with increments that follow the zoom</li><li>A «Draw» panel shared by detail lines, walls and sketches: rectangles, polygons, circles, true arcs, fillet arc, splines, ellipses, Pick Lines, Offset and Radius; the value typed while drawing</li><li>BIMopen style and dark theme at the first start, the inverted background remembered; the Classic style chosen in Options beside the BIMopen style</li><li>Stacked walls with their sub-walls, in every view</li><li>Sun and shadows in plans, sections, elevations and 3D, with the sun path and the sun study</li><li>Temporary dimensions on every element in every view, 3D included, with the references chosen and remembered</li><li>Start screen in the user's language; the ribbon complete, with the commands still to come greyed</li>","rp.steps.kicker":"Next steps","rp.steps.h2":"78 steps, in order of priority","rp.steps.p":"Each step is a complete block: commands, interface, tests, website and six languages. The order follows priority and dependencies.","rp.pr.h3":"Realigning every feature","rp.pr.p":"Before new features, every feature already built is checked again item by item, corrected and tested from the interface.","rr1.t":"Interface and navigation","rr1.d":"Aligned and tested: the ribbon with key tips (Alt), a quick access toolbar with separators and keyboard shortcuts you set, exported and imported as XML, two-letter shortcuts typed in the view, the options bar you can dock, properties, the Project Index by keyboard too with the views under each sheet, views dragged onto sheets, windows tiled by order of use, zoom towards the cursor, orbit around the selection, the orientation cube with compass and menu, and context menus in every view; every tool tried the same way in plan, elevation, section and 3D.","rr1.s":"Ready: Switch View, Close others, Tile, Cascade, Panels. Behaviours verified: 104 of 106.","st.wip":"In progress","rr2.t":"Selection and modify","rr2.d":"TAB and chains of walls, filter and Select All Instances, dragging in every view with joined walls stretching, Move, Copy, Rotate, Mirror, Repeat in Series, Align, Offset, Trim/Extend, Split, Scale and Fix, each previewed before the click like doors, windows, grids and levels (in plan, section, elevation and 3D), tested through the interface.","rr2.s":"Ready: Align, Offset, Mirror on Axis, Mirror on Line, Split Element, Move, Copy, Rotate, Shorten/Lengthen, Delete. Behaviours verified: 85 of 87.","rr3.t":"Walls, doors and windows","rr3.d":"Clean L, T and X joins with layers wrapping the corners, attaching and detaching roofs and floors, the Wall Joins tool, complete door and window symbols at every detail level. Work planes (Set, Show) and reference planes.","rr3.s":"Ready: Door, Window. Behaviours verified: 93 of 94.","rr4.t":"Floors, roofs, stairs and curtain walls","rr4.d":"Aligned and tested: sketch mode for floors and roofs with picked walls, openings, slope arrows and slope lines, and edit boundary; the profile of walls and curtain walls sketched in a section or elevation; stairs by run (with guides for the next run) or by boundary and riser lines, spiral ones too, and ramps, railings and components from the library, with the preview following the cursor. Curtain walls were aligned with R3. Monolithic runs join their landings with no step in the soffit, and railings run on over the landings as one rail. Spiral stairs and curved rails are smooth surfaces, with no lines between facets in 3D, hidden line, sections and elevations; railings have a post at every plan corner and every change of slope, on ramps too, and go round landings with acute angles without crossing. Sketch lines are selected and changed like other lines: ends dragged, Move, Offset, Trim/Extend, temporary dimensions. Wall layers and core boundaries are chosen with TAB as references for Align and Pick Lines.","rr4.s":"Ready: Stair, Railing, Object. Behaviours verified: 127 of 132.","rr5.t":"Views and graphics","rr5.d":"See-through selection in 3D, only real edges in the Lines style, slabs cutting walls without flicker, tiled windows filling the area. Graphic styles in plans and sections, cut heights with levels, per-element graphics, patterns and transparency in Visibility and Graphics, Reveal Hidden, view templates for every view. Sun and shadows in plans, sections, elevations and 3D, with the sun path and the sun study.","rr5.s":"Ready: View presets, Visibility and Graphics, Filters, Thin lines, Section, Enlarged detail, Plan, Elevation. Behaviours verified: 113 of 132.","rr6.t":"Annotation and 2D","rr6.d":"Text typed on the drawing with leaders and Find/Replace, every kind of dimension with its types, dimension text, witness lines, locks, EQ and spot elevations, tags by category and for all, rooms with limits and area and volume computations, colour schemes in the foreground and their legends, legend views, draw order of details. The «Draw» panel shared by detail lines and sketches (polygons, true arcs, fillet arc, splines, ellipses, Pick Lines, Offset and Radius); the «Snaps…» window in both styles, with increments that follow the zoom; snap overrides say where they work; a value typed in a dimension moves only walls, grids, doors and windows and detail lines; one sketch line's end drags alone, the ends of a chain chosen with TAB together; «Fillet Arc» keeps the kind of the lines it joins.","rr6.s":"Behaviours verified: 388 of 631.","rr7.t":"Documentation and files","rr7.d":"Aligned and tested: sheets with title blocks chosen and inserted with a preview following the cursor, viewports with title, rotation and the view activated on the sheet, guide grids, a sheet list with placeholder sheets, revisions and revision clouds; PDF printing with saved settings, preview, view and sheet sets, one or separate files, the 3D view and schedules too; image and IFC export with classes; units, tabbed options, project templates, transfer of project standards and opening IFC files. Done before: schedules as views linked to the model, opening, saving and backup copies.","rr7.s":"Ready: Project information, Project units, Copy Settings from Project. Behaviours verified: 166 of 168.","rp.p0.h3":"Foundations and platforms","rp.p0.p":"Quality, files, rendering and every system: the base the other steps grow on.","rb0.t":"Linux and browser","rb0.d":"Desktop version for Linux and a web version that runs in the browser, built from the same code and updated at every release.","rb0.s":"Ready: Linux desktop app, browser version.","rb1.t":"Functional testing","rb1.d":"Every command tried through the interface, on desktop and web, with automated tests; the bugs found fixed.","rb1.s":"Behaviours verified: 1149 of 1584.","rb2.t":"Graphics quality","rb2.d":"Transparent selection, only real edges in the Lines styles, no flicker at slab edges, complete openings and wall joins in plan, orbit around the selected object and zoom towards the cursor.","rb2.s":"Behaviours verified: 21 of 21.","rb3.t":"Project file as a database","rb3.d":"A database in a single file: saving writes only what changed, unsaved work is recovered after a crash, quick opening even of very large projects.","rb3.s":"Ready: project file as a database. Behaviours verified: 4 of 4.","rb4.t":"Families as files and library","rb4.d":"Loadable families saved in their own files, loaded into the project and gathered in a library.","rb4.s":"Behaviours verified: 0 of 17.","rb5.t":"Rendering engine","rb5.d":"Artificial lights and sun, shadows, textured materials, saved scenes and views, realistic images.","rb5.s":"Missing: Realistic image.","rb6.t":"Windows","rb6.d":"Desktop version for Windows.","rb6.s":"Ready: Windows desktop app.","rb7.t":"macOS","rb7.d":"Desktop version for Mac.","rb7.s":"Missing: macOS desktop app.","rb8.t":"Android","rb8.d":"App for Android tablets and phones with touch mode: an interface for finger and pen, two-finger gestures, full screen, menus and sheets fitted to the screen. Tried on a tablet and a phone; the APK can be downloaded from the test build 0.1.0-alpha.4.","rb8.s":"Ready: Android app.","rb9.t":"iPad and iPhone","rb9.d":"App for iPadOS and iOS, with the interface adapted to touch.","rb9.s":"Missing: iPadOS and iOS app.","rb10.t":"Installable web app","rb10.d":"The browser version installable with an icon, on tablets and phones too, and usable offline.","rb10.s":"Missing: installable web app.","rb11.t":"Releases for every platform","rb11.d":"Ready-to-download packages for every system, built and tested automatically at every version.","rb11.s":"Ready: Linux, Windows and Android packages; missing: automatic release from CI.","rb12.t":"User manual","rb12.d":"A step-by-step manual in six languages, on the web and in PDF, published automatically and opened from the program too (? ▸ Help, F1); each chapter is completed when its area has been realigned and tested.","rb12.s":"Ready: manual in six languages, automatic publishing of the manual.","rb13.t":"Two interface styles","rb13.d":"In Options, on the computer and in the browser, you choose the «Classic» or the «BIMopen» style; same commands, same names and keys, the choice remembered.","rb13.s":"Behaviours verified: 29 of 30.","rb14.t":"Large models","rb14.d":"From one building of a few hundred elements to real projects: incremental regeneration, spatial indexes, per-view caches and parallel work, measured at every step.","rb14.s":"Behaviours verified: 0 of 5.","rp.p1.h3":"Essential","rp.p1.p":"To draw and document a real project.","rs1.t":"Complete wall and options bar","rs1.d":"Alignment, height, constraint, offset and Continue.","rs1.s":"Ready: Wall.","rs2.t":"A common Draw panel","rs2.d":"Rectangle, polygons, circle, arcs, fillet, offset and radius for walls, floors, roofs and lines.","rs2.s":"Behaviours verified: 17 of 24.","rs3.t":"Complete selection","rs3.d":"TAB, selection filter, drag controls, «Select All Instances».","rs3.s":"Ready: Modify.","rs4.t":"Views as elements of their own","rs4.d":"Several plans per level; duplicate, rename and delete views from the Project Browser.","rs4.s":"Ready: Free 2D View, Duplicate View.","rs5.t":"Editable floor and roof boundaries","rs5.d":"Edit boundary, holes, walls picked one by one with offset.","rs5.s":"Ready: Flooring, Roof.","rs6.t":"Project materials and graphics","rs6.d":"Materials, fill patterns, line weights by scale, line patterns and subcategories.","rs6.s":"Ready: Materials, Styles by Category; missing: Divide face, Apply material.","rs7.t":"Families and types in the project","rs7.d":"Project Index by category, family and type; new type; Match Type Properties.","rs7.s":"Ready: Load Family; missing: Transfer type. Behaviours verified: 0 of 2.","rs8.t":"Text in every view and text types","rs8.d":"Notes in sections, details and sheets; font, size, leaders.","rs8.s":"Ready: Text; missing: Spell checker. Behaviours verified: 0 of 1.","rs9.t":"Tags by category and symbols","rs9.d":"Tags for rooms, walls, floors, components, roofs and stairs.","rs9.s":"Ready: Tag, Tag all, Symbol; missing: Material, Multi-category tag, Tread numbers, Stair path.","rs10.t":"Dimension types and spot dimensions","rs10.d":"Dimension types with prefix and suffix; spot elevations and coordinates.","rs10.s":"Ready: Aligned, Linear, Angular, Radial, Arc length, Spot dimension; missing: Diameter.","rs11.t":"Complete 2D details","rs11.d":"Draw order, filled regions with arcs and holes, components, repeating details and insulation.","rs11.s":"Ready: Detail line, Filled region, Detail symbol.","rs12.t":"Configurable schedules","rs12.d":"Fields, filters, sorting, grouping, formatting and editing values.","rs12.s":"Ready: Schedules. Behaviours verified: 62 of 62.","rs13.t":"Complete rooms","rs13.d":"Upper limit, room bounding, area computation rules, finishes and occupancy.","rs13.s":"Ready: Room, Room Separator, Room Label.","rs14.t":"Phases and demolition","rs14.d":"Project phases, phase filters, existing, demolished and new elements.","rs14.s":"Missing: Phases, Demolish.","rs15.t":"Ceilings and ceiling plans","rs15.d":"Automatic or sketched layered ceilings, with their own view.","rs15.s":"Missing: Ceiling. Behaviours verified: 0 of 1.","rs16.t":"Architectural columns","rs16.d":"Types, base and top levels, joining with walls.","rs16.s":"Missing: Column. Behaviours verified: 0 of 2.","rs17.t":"Complete modify tools and clipboard","rs17.d":"Scale, radial repeat in series, fix, Create Same, copy and Paste Aligned.","rs17.s":"Ready: Scale, Repeat in Series, Fix, Split with Joint, Create Same; missing: Paste, Cut, Copy, Measure.","rs18.t":"Groups","rs18.d":"Create, edit and place model and detail groups.","rs18.s":"Missing: Group, Group, 2D group, Load as group. Behaviours verified: 0 of 1.","rs19.t":"Savable 3D views","rs19.d":"Several named 3D views, the orientation cube, perspective and the section box.","rs19.s":"Ready: 3D View. Behaviours verified: 9 of 11.","rs20.t":"Complete sheets","rs20.d":"Schedules, 3D views and legends on sheets, viewports and detail references.","rs20.s":"Ready: Sheet, View, Title Block. Behaviours verified: 27 of 27.","rp.p2.h3":"Important","rp.p2.p":"To complete everyday work.","rs21.t":"Graphics by element and hidden elements","rs21.d":"Override graphics by element; reveal hidden elements.","rs21.s":"Ready: Conceal in view, Custom Graphics; missing: Show hidden lines, Remove hidden lines, Cut outline.","rs22.t":"Complete cut heights and underlay","rs22.d":"Each plane with its own level, lines beyond the cut, underlay.","rs22.s":"Behaviours verified: 5 of 6.","rs23.t":"Type properties and identity data","rs23.d":"Wall function, coarse fill pattern, type identity data.","rs23.s":"Ready: Properties.","rs24.t":"Joins and layer returns","rs24.d":"Wall joins, layer priority, vertical structure.","rs24.s":"Missing: Connect, Cut, Unjoin. Behaviours verified: 12 of 12.","rs25.t":"Sloped surfaces and openings","rs25.d":"Slope arrow, shafts, openings in walls and floors.","rs25.s":"Missing: By face, Shaft, In a wall, Vertical opening. Behaviours verified: 0 of 4.","rs26.t":"Parameters, formulas and snaps","rs26.d":"Project, shared and global parameters, formulas in schedules and types, the Snaps dialog and snap overrides.","rs26.s":"Ready: Snap, Project parameters; missing: General parameters.","rs27.t":"Curtain walls","rs27.d":"Grids, mullions and panels, in plan, 3D, schedules and IFC.","rs27.s":"Ready: Curtain Wall, Curtain grid, Mullion.","rs28.t":"Areas and color schemes","rs28.d":"Area plans, boundaries from walls, schemes by value or range, legend.","rs28.s":"Ready: Area, Area Outline, Area Label, Color legend.","rs29.t":"Complete levels and grids","rs29.d":"Types, bubbles, elbows, 2D and 3D extents.","rs29.s":"Ready: Level, Grid; missing: Extent box. Behaviours verified: 5 of 11.","rs30.t":"Reference planes, north and location","rs30.d":"Reference planes, work plane, true and project north.","rs30.s":"Ready: Define, Display, Guide plane; missing: Plane viewer, Shared coordinates, Move project. Behaviours verified: 19 of 24.","rs31.t":"Files: templates, backups and recent files","rs31.d":"New project from a template, save as template, backup copies, recent documents and save reminders.","rs31.s":"Behaviours verified: 24 of 25.","rs32.t":"DXF export and complete printing","rs32.d":"DXF/DWG with layers by category; view and sheet sets.","rs32.s":"Missing: DXF/DWG export. Behaviours verified: 15 of 15.","rs33.t":"Import and link","rs33.d":"Opening IFC files, DXF, PDF and images as a base, point clouds and link management.","rs33.s":"Ready: Insert from File; missing: Link CAD, Link PDF, Link image, Import CAD, Import PDF, Import image, Decal, Point cloud, Import gbXML. Behaviours verified: 3 of 3.","rs34.t":"Legends and dependent views","rs34.d":"Legend views, legend components, dependent views and view references.","rs34.s":"Ready: Legends; missing: View reference.","rs35.t":"Revisions and keynotes","rs35.d":"Revision clouds, revisions in the title block, keynotes from a file.","rs35.s":"Ready: Revision Cloud, Revisions; missing: Coded note.","rs36.t":"Sun and shadows","rs36.d":"Shadows, sun settings and the sun study in every view, the Realistic style.","rs36.s":"Behaviours verified: 4 of 5.","rs37.t":"Ramps and shape editing","rs37.d":"Sloped ramps; points and split lines on floors and roofs.","rs37.s":"Ready: Ramp. Behaviours verified: 0 of 4.","rs38.t":"Open 3D export","rs38.d":"glTF/OBJ and IFC2x3 besides IFC4.","rs38.s":"Missing: glTF/OBJ export, IFC2x3 export.","rp.p3.h3":"Later","rp.p3.p":"Advanced or rarer tools.","rs39.t":"Site plan","rs39.d":"Toposurface, building pads, property lines.","rs39.s":"Missing: Link topography, Terrain from face, Terrain, Site element, Parking, Building pad, Surrounding context, Divide terrain, Merge terrains, Sub-area, Property line, Grading, Contour labels.","rs40.t":"Massing and model by face","rs40.d":"Masses, mass floors, walls and roofs by face.","rs40.s":"Missing: Display masses, New mass, Place a mass, Draw in 3D, Curtain Wall, Roof, Wall, Slab.","rs41.t":"Extrusion roofs and accessories","rs41.d":"Dormers, fascias, gutters, soffits.","rs41.s":"Missing: Dormer. Behaviours verified: 0 of 4.","rs42.t":"Design options","rs42.d":"Option sets, primary option, options per view.","rs42.s":"Missing: Design options, Main version.","rs43.t":"Linked models and interference","rs43.d":"Link model, copy/monitor, interference check.","rs43.s":"Missing: Link project, Link IFC, Manage links, Federated model, Check clashes, Copy and monitor, Coordination review, Coordination options, Realign hosts, Federated model changes.","rs44.t":"Interface customisation","rs44.d":"Quick access toolbar, keyboard shortcuts with import and export, selection colours, the minimised ribbon.","rs44.s":"Behaviours verified: 9 of 10.","rs45.t":"Model text and model lines","rs45.d":"3D text and model lines on the work plane.","rs45.s":"Missing: 3D text, 3D line. Behaviours verified: 0 of 2.","rs46.t":"Family editor","rs46.d":"Parametric loadable families created and edited in BIMopen.","rs46.s":"Behaviours verified: 0 of 11.","rs47.t":"Project management tools","rs47.d":"Renumbering, the starting view, project images, saved selections, selection by number and warnings.","rs47.s":"Missing: Renumber, Opening view, Project images, Save selection, Load selection, Edit selection, Select by number, Selection numbers, Warnings.","rs48.t":"Structural elements and foundations","rs48.d":"Beams, columns, structural walls and floors, trusses, braces, beam systems, isolated, strip and slab foundations, with their tags.","rs48.s":"Missing: Beam, Structural wall, Structural column, Structural floor, Truss, Brace, Beam layout, Pad footing, Strip footing, Raft foundation, Beam tags, Span direction.","rs49.t":"Reinforcement and reinforced concrete","rs49.d":"Single, area and path reinforcement, fabric, cover, couplers, adaptive rebar and their symbols and tags.","rs49.s":"Missing: Rebar, Reinforcement over an area, Reinforcement along a path, Mesh over an area, Single mesh, Concrete cover, Coupler, Adaptive rebar, Cover options, Rebar options, Rebar tag, Rebar symbol.","rs50.t":"Steel fabrication and connections","rs50.d":"Single and automatic connections, plates, bolts, welds and the cuts and copes of steel members.","rs50.s":"Missing: Connection, Automatic joints, Plate, Bolts, Weld, Cope, Skewed cut, Shorten, Shaped cut, End cut, Corner joint, Intersection, Cut with.","rs51.t":"Parts, assemblies and precast","rs51.d":"Parts, assemblies, precast segmentation, custom fabric, shop drawings and CAM export.","rs51.s":"Missing: Divide, Assembly parts, Custom mesh, Workshop drawings, Export for CAM, Prefabrication settings, Cold-formed profiles, Suspend, Divide into parts, Create assembly.","rs52.t":"Ducts and air systems","rs52.d":"Rigid and flexible ducts, fittings, accessories, insulation, air terminals, mechanical equipment and duct legends.","rs52.s":"Missing: Duct, Duct from a path, Duct fitting, Duct accessory, Duct insulation, Flexible duct, Air terminal, Prefabricated part, Multi-point route, Duct bracing, Mechanical equipment, Control device, Duct legend.","rs53.t":"Plumbing and electrical systems","rs53.d":"Piping and plumbing fixtures, the electrical system and its loads, P&amp;ID diagrams, connections and piping legends.","rs53.s":"Ready: Modelling, Work Plane; missing: Plumbing, Electrical system, P&amp;ID editor, Disconnected connections, Electrical loads, Pipe legend.","rs54.t":"Structural analytical model","rs54.d":"Analytical members, panels and nodes, supports and boundary conditions, loads, the automatic analytical model and reading the results.","rs54.s":"Missing: Show loads, Analytical member, Analytical panel, Analytical node, Supports and restraints, Automatic analytical model, Analysis results.","rs55.t":"Spaces, zones and building analysis","rs55.d":"MEP spaces and zones with separators, names and tags, energy analysis and egress paths.","rs55.s":"Missing: Space, Space separator, Space tag, Space names, Drawn zone, Zone from spaces, Energy analysis, Escape route.","rs56.t":"Shared work","rs56.d":"Worksets, synchronisation, history, element permissions and backups, for several people working on the same project.","rs56.s":"Missing: Worksets, Synchronize, Show history, Enable sharing, Active workset, Dim other worksets, Reload changes, Release elements, Permission requests, Sharing status, Restore backup, Publishing options.","rp.cov.kicker":"Commands per tab","rp.cov.h2":"How many commands already work","rp.cov.p":"For each ribbon tab, the commands already working over the total. The others are already in place, greyed out, until they work. Last computed: 21 October 2026.","tab.viste":"Views","tab.modella":"Model","tab.modifica":"Modify","tab.annotazioni":"Annotations","tab.progetto":"Project","tab.cemento-armato":"Reinforced concrete","tab.strutture":"Structure","tab.metallo":"Metal","tab.impianti":"MEP","tab.collega-e-importa":"Link and import","tab.masse-e-sito":"Massing & site","tab.prefabbricazione":"Prefabrication","tab.verifica":"Check","tab.condividi":"Collaborate","rp.cov.total":"Total","rp.out.kicker":"Out of scope","rp.out.h2":"What BIMopen will not do","rp.out.ul":"<li>License management and proprietary online services</li><li>Proprietary material libraries and cloud rendering services</li><li>VSTA macros: in BIMopen automation goes through commands, the command line and the MCP server</li><li>Proprietary energy and structural analysis</li>","rp.cta.h2":"Try it while it grows","rp.cta.p":"Every finished step reaches the browser version right away.","rp.back":"Back to the home page","rp.meta.desc":"BIMopen's full roadmap: what works today, the steps planned by priority and how much of the planned features is already covered.","dw.meta.title":"Download BIMopen — Test build for Windows, Linux, Android and the browser","dw.kicker":"Alpha version","dw.h1":"Download BIMopen","dw.latest":"Latest version:","dw.warn.h2":"Test version, partial and not final","dw.warn.p1":"Alpha builds are incomplete and are only for trying the program. They can contain errors, change without notice and produce wrong results: <strong>do not use them for real projects or for documents with professional or legal value.</strong>","dw.warn.p2":"The software is provided “as is”, without warranties of any kind. You use it entirely at your own risk and responsibility: the author is not liable for damages, data loss or any consequence of its use.","dw.warn.p3":"<strong>Always keep a copy of your files.</strong>","dw.accept":"I have read and accept these conditions","dw.gate":"Tick the box to enable the download buttons.","dw.os.h2":"Choose your system","dw.mine":"Your system","dw.win.p":"A single executable file: download it and open it with a double click.","dw.win.btn":"Download for Windows","dw.lin.p":"A single executable file for 64-bit Linux systems: make it executable and run it.","dw.lin.btn":"Download for Linux","dw.and.p":"The app for tablets and phones, with touch mode: download the APK file on the device and open it to install the app.","dw.and.btn":"Download for Android","dw.web.p":"Opens right away, with nothing to install: you need a recent browser. Your files stay on your computer.","dw.notice":"Third-party licences (NOTICE)","dw.hint.lin":"Linux: before running it, <code>chmod +x bimopen-linux-x86_64</code>","dw.hint.win":"Windows: the .exe is not signed, so SmartScreen may stop it; choose “More info” ➤ “Run anyway”","dw.hint.and":"Android: the APK is not signed for the store; to install it, allow installing from unknown sources (unknown apps) for the browser or file manager that opens it","dw.nv.kicker":"Changelog","dw.nv.h2":"What's new","dw.nv.p":"The latest versions, newest first.","nv.added":"Added","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.added.1":"A «Reinforced concrete» ribbon tab between Structure and Metal with the reinforcement commands, in both interface styles and in touch mode.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.added.2":"Sun path aids in every view («Visual Aids»): hour lines, solar noon, the year's band between the solstices, analemmas, sunrise and sunset with their times; in 3D views the model hides the part of the path behind it.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.added.3":"The sun dragged in 3D views as in plans, «Along the Day» or «Along the Year»; sunrise, sunset and the length of the day in the view bar; the year's sunrises and sunsets as a chart in «Sun Settings», where a click picks the day.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.added.4":"Summer time follows the rule of each place and the sun's year by itself; Tokyo, São Paulo, Santiago, Sydney and Auckland join the city list.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.added.5":"Railing types with «Rail Structure (Non-Continuous)» and «Baluster Placement» (main pattern, posts at the start, corners and end), each with a preview on a sample stair.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.added.6":"«Railing ▸ Place on a host» in plans and 3D views, with «Offset from Path» and «On treads» or «On stringer».","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.added.7":"The complete «Snap» dialog, the same in both styles: length and angular increments chosen by the zoom, object snaps with their two-letter overrides, «Restore Defaults»; the settings are kept with the preferences.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.added.8":"Angle snaps in every view: a segment snaps to horizontal, vertical, parallel, perpendicular or a multiple of the angular increment, measured from the view's axis or from the previous segment, with a guide and the angle shown; in plans, sections, elevations, 3D views and sketches, also for Rotate and radial arrays.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.added.9":"«Snap Overrides» in every view where a tool takes points, typed or from the right-button menu; TAB and SHIFT+TAB go through the snaps under the cursor; «Close» (SZ) closes a chain or a sketch's loop.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.added.10":"Every ribbon drop-down lists all its ways, also found by the command search; the ways still to come are greyed as «Not available yet».","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.added.11":"Options bar: «Load Family» for doors, windows and components, «Tag on Placement» as a checkbox, «Rotate after inserting» for components, the wall's offset.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.added.12":"<code>snap</code> and <code>anglesnap</code> at the command line and through MCP.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.added.13":"In the user manual pictures open large on a click; the PDF has a cover.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.added.14":"«Keep coincident lines» in «Print Setup» prints every overlapping line instead of merging them.","nv.changed":"Changed","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.changed.1":"Dragging the sun is smooth in every view: plans, sections and elevations show a draft shadow while it moves and the full one once released; a sun study plays the same way.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.changed.2":"Shadows in 3D views have readable edges and smooth soft borders; the sunlit jamb of a window or door is lighter than the one turned away.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.changed.3":"Every dialog opens in the middle of the screen each time and keeps one size while open; what does not fit scrolls inside it.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.changed.4":"City names of the project location are shown in the interface language; files keep their location.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.changed.5":"Printed and exported sections and elevations (PDF, SVG, PNG, image export) remove hidden lines exactly.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.changed.6":"Sections and elevations paint overlapping faces in their true depth order, and window glass hides what is behind it.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.changed.7":"«On stringer» is offered only on a stair with a stringer on that side; «Place on a host» adds only the railing a side is missing.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.changed.8":"The sample house stands in Cagliari, where its address is; new projects still start in Rome.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.changed.9":"Dialogs built around long lists (materials, visibility and graphics, object styles, filters, line styles, schedule properties, parameters, keyboard shortcuts…) are resized by their edges and open again at that size; their content never resizes them.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.changed.10":"The sample house's ground floor is one continuous wall with its shop front embedded in it, as a curtain wall cuts the wall it runs along.","nv.fixed":"Fixed","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.fixed.1":"A basic wall changed to a stacked type keeps its location line: the façade no longer moves by half its thickness.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.fixed.2":"Each sub-wall of a stacked wall joins the wall beside it at its own height, with the layers closed round the corner.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.fixed.3":"Opening a project over another shows the new one in every view; every way of opening asks to save changes; saving a 3D view under a new name no longer moves the open view's camera.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.fixed.4":"Railings on stairs run on the stair's outline, posts stand whole on the steps, balusters are evenly spaced and rails no longer sink into the first tread.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.fixed.5":"Window frames no longer vanish in elevations where the sill shares their plane.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.fixed.6":"A face grazed by the sun is evenly lit, without dark streaks in 3D views and elevations.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.fixed.7":"The sun path's analemma is one smooth loop through the sun, and in perspective its lines are cut behind the eye.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.fixed.8":"Answering «No» to saving and then opening the same file reloads it as it was saved.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.fixed.9":"In 3D views the angle snap guide lies on the wall being drawn.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_5.fixed.10":"A wall's area, in schedules, material takeoffs and IFC quantities, leaves out the opening of an embedded curtain wall.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_4.added.1":"A start screen while the program loads, with the real loading stages, in the saved language, else the system's, else English; it can be turned off in Options.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_4.added.2":"Stacked walls: sub-walls drawn in every view with their own layers, set in «Type sub-walls», picked one by one with Tab and split with «Break up into single walls».","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_4.added.3":"Sun and shadows in plans, sections and elevations as in 3D views, with the sun path, «Sun Settings» and the sun study; one sun for the project or one for a view.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_4.added.4":"Temporary dimensions on every element in every view, 3D included, with witness lines anchored to any reference and remembered, and the «Temporary Dimensions» settings.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_4.added.5":"Touch mode for touch screens and pens, with two-finger gestures and layouts for tablets and phones.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_4.added.6":"Drawing in 3D views: walls, floors, roofs and sketches with the same preview, guides and temporary dimensions as in plan, and the Modify tools on sketch lines and elements.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_4.added.7":"Work planes and reference planes.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_4.added.8":"«Type layers»: the layers of a type as cards, with total thickness, thermal resistance, mass per area and a live preview.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_4.added.9":"Every ribbon tab complete: 75 commands still to come are shown greyed as «Not available yet», ten new panels among them.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_4.added.10":"A view dragged out of the drawing area opens in a window of its own, on another monitor too.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_4.added.11":"The strip of views and families with live thumbnails, and dockable Properties and Project Index panels with a type selector that shows previews.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_4.changed.1":"The wall's Properties panel and «Type Parameters» in groups, with derived values read only and rows greyed while another value does not allow them.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_4.changed.2":"Every dialog with a preview has a «Preview» switch in its header and keeps one size and place.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_4.changed.3":"The Classic style is chosen in Options beside the BIMopen one, without a separate option to enable it.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_4.changed.4":"The Classic style gets a new title bar, a ribbon that scrolls instead of cutting buttons off, one options bar and no status bar.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_4.changed.5":"The main window fills the screen at the first start; later it opens as it was closed.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_4.changed.6":"The orientation cube has bevelled facets and arrows around it, and more contrast on light and dark backgrounds.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_4.changed.7":"Hidden line keeps white faces and dark lines in both themes; the shaded styles fill plans and sections with the materials' colours.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_4.changed.8":"Colours and patterns come from the material alone, in every view and every preview.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_4.changed.9":"Stair and ramp railings follow the stair's boundary on each side from the start; curved stairs and rails are smooth surfaces.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_4.changed.10":"Functions not available yet are greyed in both interface styles.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_4.changed.11":"The user manual shows the BIMopen style; its «Interface styles» chapter shows the Classic style and touch mode on a monitor, a tablet and a phone.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_4.fixed.1":"The 3D view draws walls, floors, roofs and frames without hairline cracks.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_4.fixed.2":"Door and window frames no longer overlap at their corners: no flicker in 3D, no stray lines in sections and elevations.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_4.fixed.3":"The first-floor slab of the sample house stops at the walls' core, behind the insulation.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_4.fixed.4":"No spikes at the edges of the orientation cube.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_4.fixed.5":"On Wayland the main window no longer closes after the start screen.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_4.fixed.6":"A panel made floating is no longer drawn twice.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_4.fixed.7":"Openings keep their wall at corners and when copied; a click on a window's glass picks the window in sections, elevations and 3D.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_3.changed.1":"The BIMopen interface style at the first start; the Classic style stays once chosen in Options.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_3.changed.2":"In a sketch, the end of a line selected on its own drags alone; with a chain selected (Tab) the ends where its lines meet drag together.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_3.changed.3":"The snap settings open from both interface styles; snap overrides say where they can be used.","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_3.fixed.1":"A fillet arc keeps the kind of the sketch lines it joins (a boundary stays a boundary, not a riser).","nv.v0_1_0_alpha_3.fixed.2":"A typed dimension value moves only walls, grids, doors, windows and detail lines.","dw.meta.desc":"Download the test (alpha) build of BIMopen for Windows 10/11, Linux and Android, or open it in the browser with nothing to install. A partial, non-final version, only for trying the program.","e404.title":"Page not found — BIMopen","e404.h1":"This page does not exist","e404.p":"The address is wrong or the page has moved.","e404.btn":"Back to BIMopen"};
